  "description": "and you'll want to sigh, \"Ahhhhhhh-luminum.\"\nThat's because the Sunfire's frame is crafted from 7005 aluminum. It has\na PowerDiamond downtube to help more of your pedal power make it to the\nground and fewer of your fillings to get loosened by rough riding surfaces.\nIt has the elegant and functional Fuji Edge S-bend MonoStay connecting\nthe seat tube and stays and a replaceable rear derailleur hanger so you\ndon't have to toss your entire frame when the Fickle Finger of Fate plants\na derailleur-eating rock in your path.\n\nBecause of all that aluminum wonderfulness, the Sunfire costs about half\na C-note more than its cousin, Odessa, but weighs about two pounds less.\nThat \"Ahhhhhh-luminum\" easy feeling is augmented with Shimano\neight-speed gearing. It's like having an 8.5-iron in your golf bag or\nsix fingers for guitar playing. Not cheating, exactly, but an advantage\nnonetheless.\n\nSunfire isn't quite a full-time off-roader, but it's quite capable of\ndelivering you to a good time on your favorite trails. Slap a rack on\nthe back and you can also press it into occasional weekend touring service.\nIt's versatile. It's a bargain. It's \"Ahhhhhh-luminum.",
